x.\n*****************************************************************************\nSURNAME             FIRST NAME                AGE     IMAGE       BEAT    \n\nBatterly            Louisa                    28      0244b   Canton Beat\nBatterly            Richmond                  26      0244b   Canton Beat\n\nNO"], "famc": [], "fams": ["@F106@", "@F107@"]}, "@I295@": {"id": "@I295@", "name": "Susan Mijues", "given": "Susan", "surname": "Mijues", "sex": "F", "birth": {"date": "ABT  1845", "place": "Georgia"}, "death": {"date": "1910", "place": "Canton Beat, Texas"}, "burial": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "occupation": [], "education": [], "notes": ["CENSUS RECORDS - SMITH COUNTY, TX - INDEX FOR 1870 US CENSUS\n\nSURNAMES:  MIJUES - MYSON\n\nSubmitted by East Texas Genealogical Society\nP. O. Box 6967, Tyler, TX 75711\n\nCopyright.  All rights reserved.\nhttp://usgwarchives.net/copyright.htm\n\n***********************************************************************\n\nThanks to Dan Milligan and Juanice York for copyingthe Index and \nEdith Willman and Nancy Crain for proofreading the index.\n\n*****************************************************************************\nSURNAME             FIRST NAME                AGE     IMAGE       BEAT\nNO\n*****************************************************************************\n\nMijues              Hannah1       0244b   Canton Beat\nMijues              Horatio4       0244b   Canton Beat\nMijues              Susan25      0244b   Canton Beat\nMijues              William6       0244b   Canton Beat"], "famc": [], "fams": ["@F106@", "@F108@", "@F109@"]}, "@I296@": {"id": "@I296@", "name": "Unknown D.", "given": "Unknown", "surname": "D.", "sex": "M", "birth": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "death": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "burial": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "occupation": [], "education": [], "notes": [], "famc": [], "fams": ["@F108@"], "living": true}, "@I297@": {"id": "@I297@", "name": "William `Bill` Johnson", "given": "William `Bill`", "surname": "Johnson", "sex": "M", "birth": {"date": "1927", "place": ""}, "death": {"date": "Sep", "place": ""}, "burial": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "occupation": [], "education": [], "notes": ["William “Bill” Johnson is listed in the 1880 Census Report as  black. The 1910 Census Report listed him as mulatto. According to  family members, he was part black and part white with blue eyes and  looked like a white man. He was known tocurse prolifically. He was  born in 1854 or 1855 in Texas. His father was born in South  Carolina; his mother was born in Georgia.  William Johnson died September 27, 1927.  The following information is recorded in the 1880 Census Report.The information going across for each person) is: name, color/race,  gender, age, relation to head of household, occupation, place of birth,  place of birth offather, and place of birth of mother.  Johnson, William B M 26 Head Farming TX --  Johnson, Susan B F 35 Wife Housekeeping GA - -  Johnson, Anna B F 11 Daughter Farm Laborer TX - -  Johnson, Theodoshius B M 7 Son - TX - -  Johnson, J.H.B.B M 5 Son - TX - -  According to family members, William and Susan’s children were:  1. Anna Johnson, b. 1869  2. Theodoshius Johnson, b. 1872/73  3. John HenryJohnson, b. 1874/75  4. Susan “Susie” Johnson, b. May 1,1882, d. May 10,1974  5. Dosheres Johnson"], "famc": [], "fams": ["@F109@"]}, "@I304@": {"id": "@I304@", "name": "Fred C.", "given": "Fred", "surname": "C.", "sex": "M", "birth": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "death": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "burial": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "occupation": [], "education": [], "notes": [], "famc": [], "fams": ["@F110@"], "living": true}, "@I312@": {"id": "@I312@", "name": "Unknown U.", "given": "Unknown", "surname": "U.", "sex": "M", "birth": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "death": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "burial": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "occupation": [], "education": [], "notes": [], "famc": [], "fams": ["@F111@"], "living": true}, "@I306@": {"id": "@I3