s", "sex": "M", "birth": {"date": "Jun 25 1911", "place": "Tyler, Texas"}, "death": {"date": "Jul 30 1970", "place": "Tyler, Texas"}, "burial": {"date": "Aug 02 1970", "place": ""}, "occupation": [], "education": [], "notes": [], "famc": ["@F200@"], "fams": ["@F191@"]}, "@I31@": {"id": "@I31@", "name": "Edmond Battles", "given": "Edmond", "surname": "Battles", "sex": "M", "birth": {"date": "May 1897", "place": "Tyler, Texas"}, "death": {"date": "Aug 1957", "place": "Tyler, Texas"}, "burial": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "occupation": [], "education": [], "notes": [], "famc": ["@F200@"], "fams": ["@F116@", "@F117@", "@F118@"]}, "@I32@": {"id": "@I32@", "name": "Settie Alma Battles", "given": "Settie Alma", "surname": "Battles", "sex": "F", "birth": {"date": "Sep 05 1898", "place": "Tyler, Texas"}, "death": {"date": "Dec 1991", "place": "Fort Worth, Texas"}, "burial": {"date": "Dec 13 1991", "place": ""}, "occupation": [], "education": [], "notes": [], "famc": ["@F200@"], "fams": ["@F6@"]}, "@I33@": {"id": "@I33@", "name": "Sam Calvin Battles", "given": "Sam Calvin", "surname": "Battles", "sex": "M", "birth": {"date": "Mar 12 1900", "place": "Tyler, Texas"}, "death": {"date": "Nov 27 1972", "place": "Fort Worth, Texas"}, "burial": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "occupation": [], "education": [], "notes": [], "famc": ["@F200@"], "fams": ["@F201@", "@F202@"]}, "@I34@": {"id": "@I34@", "name": "Johnnie Mae Battles", "given": "Johnnie Mae", "surname": "Battles", "sex": "F", "birth": {"date": "Jan 05 1903", "place": "Smith County, Texas"}, "death": {"date": "Mar 25 1974", "place": "Tyler, Texas"}, "burial": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "occupation": [], "education": [], "notes": [], "famc": ["@F200@"], "fams": ["@F8@"]}, "@I35@": {"id": "@I35@", "name": "Augustus `Gus` Battles", "given": "Augustus `Gus`", "surname": "Battles", "sex": "M", "birth": {"date": "Jan 28 1905", "place": "Tyler, Texas"}, "death": {"date": "Dec 1965", "place": "Fort Worth, Texas"}, "burial": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "occupation": [], "education": [], "notes": ["Superintendent Gus Battles was born January 28, 1905 in Tyler, Smith County, Texas to the parentage of Mr. and Mrs. Horatio Battles.     Gus lived with his parents until the age of thirteen when he left Tyler and moved to Fort Worth, Texas.Gus and Miss Angie Wallace were united in marriage, July 25, 1922. To thisunion five children were born, two of which preceded Gus in death.      Gus confessed to Christ and received the Baptism of the Holy Ghost under the leadershipof Elder C. Olga Love in 1923, where Gus served faithfully as a member. He became a licensed and ordained minister under the leadership of Bishop E. E. Hamilton and served as his assistant pastor for five years and assistant pastor under the leadership of Bishop S.D. Lee at the Love Chapel C.O.G.I.C. for seven years until he heard the call to go into another vineyard to watch over the flocks of the master.    Gus’s first pastorate was at the Vickery Blvd. Church of God in Christ, where he served faithfully and God blessed his work. He felt the urgency to build God a house, and they moved to 1020 Bryan Street on the Southside in Fort Worth, Texas. The church was named Love Sanctuary C.O.G.I.C., and Gus served as a faithful and loyal servant until his home going.  He was also called to Grapevine, Texas to pastor, and for fifteen years, he served as shepherd of the flock and built a church and left it free of indebtedness.     During his pastorate,Gus held the following positions: President of the Fort Worth District Y. P. W.W., Treasurer of the State Youth Department of Texas N. E., and Superintendentof the Stop-Six District.      Gus was one of the first three Negroes to be a licensed and bonded as a contractor by the City of Fort Worth.     Battles and Sons Cement Contractors was established in 1947."], "famc": ["@F200@"], "fams": ["@F203@"]}, "@I36@": {"id": "@I36@", "name": "Clemie Battles", "given": "Clemie", "surname": "Battles", "sex": "M", "birth": {"date": "1906", "place": "Tyler, Texas"}, "death": {"date": "1920", "place": "Tyler, Texas"}, "burial": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "occupation": [], "education": [], "notes": ["According to the 1910 Census Report, which was taken on May, 1910, Clemie was 4years old.  According to the 1920 Census Report, which was taken on January 1, 1920, Clemie was 13 years old.  According to an entry in the family bible, Clemiedied in 1920."], "famc": ["@F200@"], "fams": []}, "@I37@": {"id": "@I37@", "name": "Luther `Chap` Battles", "given": "Luther `Chap`", "surname": "Battles", "sex": "M", "birth": {"date": "1908", "place": "Tyler, Texas"}, "death": {"date": "Oct 19 1930", "place": "Tyler, Texas"}, "burial": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "occupation": [], "education": [], "notes": ["Luther’s death followed an accident in which he had attempted to jump onto the side of a Model-T  Ford to hitch a ride to town in Tyler with two or three othermen. Luther missed catching onto the car  as he attempted to jump on and fell tothe street. Shortly after the accident, he became ill and was  treated by Dr. William F. Warren, Lizzie’s doctor. Luther died from internal bleeding"], "famc": ["@F200@"], "fams": []}, "@I38@": {"id": "@I38@", "name": "L.J. Battles", "given": "L.J.", "surname": "Battles", "sex": "M", "birth": {"date": "Mar 09 1915", "place": "Tyler, Texas"}, "death": {"date": "Feb 1984", "place": "Fort Worth, Texas"}, "burial": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "occupation": [], "education": [], "notes": [], "famc": ["@F200@"], "fams": ["@F74@", "@F75@"]}, "@I39@": {"id": "@I39@", "name": "Nathaniel Battles", "given": "Nathaniel", "surname": "Battles", "sex": "M", "birth": {"date": "1918", "place": "Tyler, Texas"}, "death": {"date": "Oct 01 1952", "place": ""}, "burial": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "occupation": [], "education": [], "notes": ["Nathaniel met Carrie in 1938 while he was living with his brother, L.J., and their father, Horatio at  Jack Yancey’s Place on Ark Road in Tyler, Texas. Nathaniel and Carrie lived with Horatio until they  moved to Fort Worth in 1948.  Nathaniel could play the piano and the organ by ear"], "famc": ["@F200@"], "fams": ["@F133@"]}, "@I422@": {"id": "@I422@", "name": "Anthony B.", "given": "Anthony", "surname": "B.", "sex": "M", "birth": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "death": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "burial": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "occupation": [], "education": [], "notes": [], "famc": ["@F132@"], "fams": ["@F135@"], "living": true}, "@I423@": {"id": "@I423@", "name": "Easter B.", "given": "Easter", "surname": "B.", "sex": "F", "birth": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "death": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "burial": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "occupation": [], "education": [], "notes": [], "famc": ["@F132@"], "fams": [], "living": true}, "@I377@": {"id": "@I377@", "name": "R.B. Battles", "given": "R.B.", "surname": "Battles", "sex": "M", "birth": {"date": "Jan 24 1947", "place": "Tyler, Texas"}, "death": {"date": "Jun 05 2001", "place": "Tyler, Texas"}, "burial": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "occupation": [], "education": [], "notes": [], "famc": ["@F118@"], "fams": ["@F115@"]}, "@I375@": {"id": "@I375@", "name": "Tommy Lee Battles", "given": "Tommy Lee", "surname": "Battles", "sex": "M", "birth": {"date": "Aug 02 1943", "place": ""}, "death": {"date": "Oct 11 2000", "place": ""}, "burial": {"date": "Nov 2000", "place": ""}, "occupation": [], "education": [], "notes": [], "famc": ["@F118@"], "fams": []}, "@I376@": {"id": "@I376@", "name": "Easter B.", "given": "Easter", "surname": "B.", "sex": "F", "birth": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "death": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "burial": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "occupation": [], "education": [], "notes": [], "famc": ["@F118@"], "fams": ["@F134@"], "living": true}, "@I425@": {"id": "@I425@", "name": "Gladus Battles", "given": "Gladus", "surname": "Battles", "sex": "F", "birth": {"date": "ABT  1925", "place": "Smith County, Texas"}, "death": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "burial": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "occupation": [], "education": [], "notes": [], "famc": ["@F117@"], "fams": []}, "@I102@": {"id": "@I102@", "name": "Johnnie Calvin Battles", "given": "Johnnie Calvin", "surname": "Battles", "sex": "M", "birth": {"date": "Jul 12 1918", "place": "Tyler, Texas"}, "death": {"date": "May 18 1974", "place": "Tyler, Texas"}, "burial": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "occupation": [], "education": [], "notes": ["He was buried at Oliver Chapel Cementary"], "famc": ["@F201@"], "fams": ["@F76@", "@F31@"]}, "@I103@": {"id": "@I103@", "name": "Maxine Battles", "given": "Maxine", "surname": "Battles", "sex": "F", "birth": {"date": "1920", "place": ""}, "death": {"date": "1938", "place": "Tyler, Texas"}, "burial": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "occupation": [], "education": [], "notes": ["She was buried at Oliver Chapel Cementary"], "famc": ["@F201@"], "fams": []}, "@I104@": {"id": "@I104@", "name": "Costromia `Cos` Battles", "given": "Costromia `Cos`", "surname": "Battles", "sex": "M", "birth": {"date": "Dec 01 1922", "place": "Tyler, Texas"}, "death": {"date": "Feb 27 1985", "place": "Tyler, Texas"}, "burial": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "occupation": [], "education": [], "notes": ["He was buried at Oliver Chapel Cementary"], "famc": ["@F201@"], "fams": ["@F46@"]}, "@I135@": {"id": "@I135@", "name": "Augustus Battles/ Jr.", "given": "Augustus", "surname": "Battles/ Jr.", "sex": "M", "birth": {"date": "Aug 23 1932", "place": "Tyler, Texas"}, "death": {"date": "Feb 25 1933", "place": "Tyler, Texas"}, "burial": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "occupation": [], "education": [], "notes": [], "famc": ["@F203@"], "fams": []}, "@I132@": {"id": "@I132@", "name": "Edward Lee Battles", "given": "Edward Lee", "surname": "Battles", "sex": "M", "birth": {"date": "Dec 31 1923", "place": "Fort Worth, Texas"}, "death": {"date": "Dec 11 1996", "place": ""}, "burial": {"date": "", "place": ""}, "occupation": [], "education": [], "notes": ["Known as “Uncle Buddy” to his nephews and nieces, and “Paw Paw” to his  grandchildren, Edward could play the trumpet, piano, harmonica, and  guitar.  Edward’s pastoral career began in Mansfield in 1945. On April 27, 1947, he received his certificate of  ordination. In 1948, he was appointed pastor of the Arlington Church of God in Christ, and under him  a new church, Emanuel, was built. In 1958, he was appointed pastor of the Mitchell Street Church of  God in Christ in Dallas, Texas.  In 1965, Edward succeeded his father, Superintendent Gus Battles, founder of Love Sanctuary, as  pastor of Love Sanctuary in Fort Worth. Edward successfully pastored both churches. Under his  leadership, Love Sanctuary purchased amodern structure. The Mitchell Street Church of God in Christ  changed its nameto Abundant Life and a new edifice was built.  In addition to leading two congregations, Edward made important strides at the local, state, and  national levels of the Church of God in Christ. He served as district superintendent of the Fort Worth  Metroplex District for 14 years as well as superintendent of the StopSix District, Texas Northeast. For  18 years, he worked faithfully as vice president and president of the youth department. At the time of  his demise, he was actively leading the International Department of Evangelism as president. His  community experience included membership on the boards of the Sickle Cell Anemia Foundation and  the Maddox Community Center Council. He was a member of the Interdenominational Ministerial  Alliance and was a lifetime member of the NAACP."], "famc": ["@F203@"], "fams": ["@F30@", "@F29@"]}, "@I133@": {"id": "@I133@", "name": "Milton Augustus Battles", "given": "Milton Augustus", "surname": "Battles", "sex": "M", "birth": {"date": "Jul 19 1925", "place": "Fort Worth, Texas"}, "death": {"date": "Jan 14 1980", "place": "Fort Worth, Texas"}, "burial": {"date": "Jan 18 1980", "place": ""}, "occupation": [], "education": [], "notes": [], "famc": ["@F203@"], "fams": ["@F79@", "@F8